{"id":"refine_20260928163839868","summary":"Updated the global task memory with the validated rule to preserve complete framed tiles in the output.","rationale":"The initial bare-tile output was incorrect; preserving the frame and separators in the selected tiles produced the confirmed correct answer.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this task should return the selected complete tiles, including their frames, stacked in original tile-row order; validate that three 5×5 tiles yield a 19×7 output.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_6b14fc71_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-6b14fc71 rule","content":"For task-6b14fc71, the input is a grid of framed 5×5 symbol tiles arranged in tile rows. In each tile row, identify the unique odd-pattern tile. Stack the selected complete tiles vertically in original tile-row order, preserving the frame color and separators; do not output only the bare tile interiors. For three tile rows, the result is 19×7 (three 5×5 interiors plus framing and separators), not 15×5. This output format was confirmed by a correct submission.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Corrects the existing task memory with the validated complete-tile output format, which fixed an incorrect bare-tile submission.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_6b14fc71_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-6b14fc71 rule","content":"For task-6b14fc71, the input is a grid of framed 5x5 symbol tiles arranged in several tile rows. In each tile row, exactly one tile is the odd pattern; extract that tile. Stack the odd tiles vertically in original tile-row order, preserving the input frame/separator color and tile contents. Verified on a 3x3 demo and a 3x4 test; the predicted 19x7 output was accepted.","path":"continual_arc/task-6b14fc71","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"source":"solved instance with demo","confidence":"high"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-28T16:31:05.083175+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-28T16:31:05.083192+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_6b14fc71_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-6b14fc71 rule","content":"For task-6b14fc71, the input is a grid of framed 5×5 symbol tiles arranged in tile rows. In each tile row, identify the unique odd-pattern tile. Stack the selected complete tiles vertically in original tile-row order, preserving the frame color and separators; do not output only the bare tile interiors. For three tile rows, the result is 19×7 (three 5×5 interiors plus framing and separators), not 15×5. This output format was confirmed by a correct submission.","path":"continual_arc/task-6b14fc71","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T16:31:05.083175+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-28T16:38:44.112Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260928191252725","summary":"Created a global memory recording the validated rule for Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1.","rationale":"The pairing and composition rule was supported by both demonstrations and a correct test submission, making it a stable, task-specific lesson for future instances.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-9f5e21c1 should pair panels and objects by the number of 4-connected background-hole components and construct the composite tiles in panel row-major order.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_9f5e21c1_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1 rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1, large square panels are base-color templates with background-colored holes, and smaller patterned objects also contain background-colored holes. Count 4-connected components of background holes in each panel and object; pair objects with panels having the same component count. Output the composites in the panels’ original row-major arrangement, retaining each panel’s one-cell base-color border and placing the matched object in its interior with the object’s background-hole cells replaced by the panel color. This rule was validated by both demos and a correct test submission.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-9f5e21c1"},"reason":"Preserves the validated task-specific transformation for future instances.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_9f5e21c1_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1 rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1, large square panels are base-color templates with background-colored holes, and smaller patterned objects also contain background-colored holes. Count 4-connected components of background holes in each panel and object; pair objects with panels having the same component count. Output the composites in the panels’ original row-major arrangement, retaining each panel’s one-cell base-color border and placing the matched object in its interior with the object’s background-hole cells replaced by the panel color. This rule was validated by both demos and a correct test submission.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-9f5e21c1"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T19:13:02.191Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T19:13:02.191Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260928191709831","summary":"Updated the global task-9f5e21c1 memory with the demo-validated matching and composition procedure.","rationale":"The two demonstrations establish that panels and objects are paired by the number of 4-connected background-hole components; the object is centered in the panel, its background holes become the panel base color, and panel holes are used only for matching.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should produce correctly composed panel-sized tiles in the panels’ original row-major arrangement; validate by checking the centered object, filled object holes, and tile ordering against the demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_9f5e21c1_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1 rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1, large square panels are base-color templates with background-colored holes, and smaller patterned objects also contain background-colored holes. Count 4-connected components of background holes in each panel and object, then pair panels and objects with equal counts. Center each object in its paired panel. Construct a panel-sized output tile using the panel's base color throughout, then preserve the object's non-background-colored cells at the centered position; object's background holes are filled with the panel base color. Ignore the panel's own hole pixels when composing the tile; they are used only for matching. Arrange the composite tiles in the panels' original row-major layout.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Both provided demonstrations support these matching and composition details, clarifying that panel holes do not carry into the output.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_9f5e21c1_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1 rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1, large square panels are base-color templates with background-colored holes, and smaller patterned objects also contain background-colored holes. Count 4-connected components of background holes in each panel and object; pair objects with panels having the same component count. Output the composites in the panels’ original row-major arrangement, retaining each panel’s one-cell base-color border and placing the matched object in its interior with the object’s background-hole cells replaced by the panel color. This rule was validated by both demos and a correct test submission.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-9f5e21c1"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T19:13:02.191Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T19:13:02.191Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_9f5e21c1_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1 rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-9f5e21c1, large square panels are base-color templates with background-colored holes, and smaller patterned objects also contain background-colored holes. Count 4-connected components of background holes in each panel and object, then pair panels and objects with equal counts. Center each object in its paired panel. Construct a panel-sized output tile using the panel's base color throughout, then preserve the object's non-background-colored cells at the centered position; object's background holes are filled with the panel base color. Ignore the panel's own hole pixels when composing the tile; they are used only for matching. Arrange the composite tiles in the panels' original row-major layout.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T19:13:02.191Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T19:17:15.754Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260928192047342","summary":"Created a global memory for Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca’s validated framed-tile movement rule.","rationale":"A demonstration established the behavior, and applying it to the test produced a correct submission.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-cc2878ca can preserve each tile’s contents while moving it in the direction indicated by its frame color.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_cc2878ca_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca, the grid contains complete 5×5 framed tiles, each with a 3×3 center. Keep each tile’s rows, frame, and center unchanged. Tiles framed in color 8 slide horizontally left; tiles framed in color 2 slide horizontally right, stopping at the canvas edge or another tile when their vertical spans overlap. Treat the background as empty space. A demo-supported application of this rule produced a correct test submission.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Persist the demonstrated and test-validated task-specific rule for future instances.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cc2878ca_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca, the grid contains complete 5×5 framed tiles, each with a 3×3 center. Keep each tile’s rows, frame, and center unchanged. Tiles framed in color 8 slide horizontally left; tiles framed in color 2 slide horizontally right, stopping at the canvas edge or another tile when their vertical spans overlap. Treat the background as empty space. A demo-supported application of this rule produced a correct test submission.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T19:20:51.673Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T19:20:51.673Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260928194412929","summary":"Updated the global task-cc2878ca memory with the validated same-color blocking rule.","rationale":"The demos and successful test show that tiles block only other tiles in the same movement class when their vertical spans overlap; opposite-color tiles can pass each other. The broader blocker assumption led to two incorrect submissions.","expectedOutcome":"Future solutions for task-cc2878ca should preserve complete 5×5 tiles and the background, move color-8 tiles left and color-2 tiles right, and allow opposite-color tiles to cross; validate against the demonstrations and test behavior.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_cc2878ca_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca framed-tile movement rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca, the grid contains complete 5×5 framed tiles, each with a 3×3 center. Preserve every tile’s rows, frame, center, and the background. Tiles framed in color 8 slide horizontally left; tiles framed in color 2 slide horizontally right. When vertical spans overlap, a tile is blocked only by another tile in the same frame-color/movement class. Opposite-color tiles do not block one another and may pass or cross despite overlapping vertical spans. Demo evidence and a correctly solved test validate this rule. A broader assumption that any tile blocks movement caused two incorrect submissions.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Validated by demonstrations and successful test submission"},"reason":"Capture the validated collision behavior and the specific failure of the broader blocker assumption.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cc2878ca_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca, the grid contains complete 5×5 framed tiles, each with a 3×3 center. Keep each tile’s rows, frame, and center unchanged. Tiles framed in color 8 slide horizontally left; tiles framed in color 2 slide horizontally right, stopping at the canvas edge or another tile when their vertical spans overlap. Treat the background as empty space. A demo-supported application of this rule produced a correct test submission.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T19:20:51.673Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T19:20:51.673Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_cc2878ca_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca framed-tile movement rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-cc2878ca, the grid contains complete 5×5 framed tiles, each with a 3×3 center. Preserve every tile’s rows, frame, center, and the background. Tiles framed in color 8 slide horizontally left; tiles framed in color 2 slide horizontally right. When vertical spans overlap, a tile is blocked only by another tile in the same frame-color/movement class. Opposite-color tiles do not block one another and may pass or cross despite overlapping vertical spans. Demo evidence and a correctly solved test validate this rule. A broader assumption that any tile blocks movement caused two incorrect submissions.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Validated by demonstrations and successful test submission"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T19:20:51.673Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T19:44:17.268Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260928204456970","summary":"Created a global memory for the validated single-marker rule in Continual-ARC task-a4019f09.","rationale":"The left- and right-edge single-marker cases were demonstrated, and the rule produced a correct test submission; multi-marker behavior is explicitly excluded.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-a4019f09 with one edge marker should preserve the cut-line pattern, recolor the ray to the farthest 7, and move the two off-line regions to their corresponding corners; validate by checking bounding-box alignment and unchanged background.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_a4019f09_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-a4019f09 single-edge-marker rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a4019f09 when there is exactly one color-2 marker on an edge, the marker defines a row or column cut line. Keep color-7 cells on that line in place. From the marker toward the grid interior, recolor background cells along the line to 2 through the farthest encountered 7; preserve those 7 cells and leave cells beyond the farthest 7 unchanged. Move all 7 cells strictly on each side of the line as rigid patterns into the corresponding two corners on the marker's side, aligning each region's bounding box to its destination corner and clearing its original cells. Preserve the background elsewhere. This rule was validated for left- and right-edge markers and by a correct test submission. Do not infer behavior for multiple markers from this rule.","path":"continual_arc/task-a4019f09","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Records the demonstrated single-marker transformation for reuse while explicitly limiting the rule to cases supported by the evidence.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_a4019f09_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-a4019f09 single-edge-marker rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-a4019f09 when there is exactly one color-2 marker on an edge, the marker defines a row or column cut line. Keep color-7 cells on that line in place. From the marker toward the grid interior, recolor background cells along the line to 2 through the farthest encountered 7; preserve those 7 cells and leave cells beyond the farthest 7 unchanged. Move all 7 cells strictly on each side of the line as rigid patterns into the corresponding two corners on the marker's side, aligning each region's bounding box to its destination corner and clearing its original cells. Preserve the background elsewhere. This rule was validated for left- and right-edge markers and by a correct test submission. Do not infer behavior for multiple markers from this rule.","path":"continual_arc/task-a4019f09","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T20:45:04.022Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T20:45:04.022Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260928212759253","summary":"Created a global memory for the validated Continual-ARC task-5024d828 panel-and-piece tiling rule.","rationale":"The rule was validated on two demonstrations and the test: source-piece footprints tile the target cells without rotation, while preserving each piece’s colors and orientation and the panel’s base color.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can identify the target panel and source pieces, fill the target cells by matching footprints, and return the completed panel crop; validate by checking that every target cell is covered exactly once and no piece is rotated or altered.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_5024d828_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-5024d828 panel-and-piece tiling rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-5024d828, identify the target panel and the colored source pieces. The source-piece footprints tile the target cells exactly without rotation. Preserve each piece’s colors and orientation, place pieces by matching their footprints to the target cells, retain the panel’s base/background color, and return only the completed target panel crop. In the validated 15×15 test, the target was the 15×7 left region: color 4 was the panel base and color 7 marked target cells. Source pieces on the color-7 background—a 2×5 color-1 rectangle, 6×2 color-6 rectangle, 2×2 color-2 rectangle, two 1×4 color-8 bars, 3×2 color-3 rectangle, and a color-0 singleton—tiled those cells.","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"validated on two demonstrations and the test"},"reason":"Preserves the demonstrated task rule and a concrete test example for recurring instances.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_5024d828_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-5024d828 panel-and-piece tiling rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-5024d828, identify the target panel and the colored source pieces. The source-piece footprints tile the target cells exactly without rotation. Preserve each piece’s colors and orientation, place pieces by matching their footprints to the target cells, retain the panel’s base/background color, and return only the completed target panel crop. In the validated 15×15 test, the target was the 15×7 left region: color 4 was the panel base and color 7 marked target cells. Source pieces on the color-7 background—a 2×5 color-1 rectangle, 6×2 color-6 rectangle, 2×2 color-2 rectangle, two 1×4 color-8 bars, 3×2 color-3 rectangle, and a color-0 singleton—tiled those cells.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"validated on two demonstrations and the test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-28T21:28:05.471Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T21:28:05.471Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929000827728","summary":"Created a global memory for the validated Continual-ARC task-e3fa3d5b rule.","rationale":"The demonstration and correctly solved test support a reusable rule: count each colored motif outside the output panel and repeat its seed marker horizontally according to that count.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-e3fa3d5b should return the output-panel crop with each seed repeated at every other column, matching the count of corresponding external motifs; validate against the demonstrated and test counts.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_e3fa3d5b_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-e3fa3d5b motif-count panel rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-e3fa3d5b, identify the zero-filled output panel containing one seed marker per relevant color on alternating rows. Outside the panel, count the repeated motifs of each seed color. Return the panel crop, repeating each seed horizontally at every other column so its total number of markers equals the number of corresponding external motifs. Demonstration counts: color 8 = 3, color 4 = 1, color 2 = 2. Validated test counts: color 1 = 2, color 2 = 2, color 8 = 4, color 3 = 5.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The demonstration and correct test submission validate this task-specific transformation and its motif-count mapping.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_e3fa3d5b_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-e3fa3d5b motif-count panel rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-e3fa3d5b, identify the zero-filled output panel containing one seed marker per relevant color on alternating rows. Outside the panel, count the repeated motifs of each seed color. Return the panel crop, repeating each seed horizontally at every other column so its total number of markers equals the number of corresponding external motifs. Demonstration counts: color 8 = 3, color 4 = 1, color 2 = 2. Validated test counts: color 1 = 2, color 2 = 2, color 8 = 4, color 3 = 5.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:08:33.840Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T00:08:33.840Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929001129643","summary":"Created a global memory for the validated Continual-ARC task-864f4116 rule.","rationale":"The three demonstrations and the correct test submission support the supplied rule for ranking endpoint-color bars and recoloring a bounded portion of the selected bar.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-864f4116 should rank matching vertical bars by interior length, recolor the rank-selected bar as specified, and preserve all other cells; validate the result against the demonstrations and grid structure.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_864f4116_rule","title":"Continual-ARC task-864f4116 ranked-bar recoloring rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-864f4116, the upper-left key gives, for each endpoint color, a rank equal to the count of that color in its key shape. Find vertical bars whose endpoints share that color and whose interior is a uniform different color; sort those bars by interior length descending and select the rank-th. Recolor the selected bar's interior from its upper endpoint downward with the endpoint color, for up to the numeric value of the interior color, bounded by the segment length. Preserve all other cells. This rule is supported by the three demonstrations and a correct test submission.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Records a validated, reusable task-specific transformation rule supported by demonstrations and a correct test result.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_864f4116_rule","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-864f4116 ranked-bar recoloring rule","content":"For Continual-ARC task-864f4116, the upper-left key gives, for each endpoint color, a rank equal to the count of that color in its key shape. Find vertical bars whose endpoints share that color and whose interior is a uniform different color; sort those bars by interior length descending and select the rank-th. Recolor the selected bar's interior from its upper endpoint downward with the endpoint color, for up to the numeric value of the interior color, bounded by the segment length. Preserve all other cells. This rule is supported by the three demonstrations and a correct test submission.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:11:33.404Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T00:11:33.404Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790545239/attempts/b0bc2d8c83274835bc96e5cf211d4242/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
